= ψ Boundary Conditions =

ψ boundary conditions are the link between [[ψ Dispersion Relations]] — which specify what ψ waves can propagate in an infinite medium — and the finite-geometry engineering reality of every [[Psi-Tech]] device. The dispersion relation gives a continuous spectrum of allowed frequencies for infinite media. Boundaries cut that continuous spectrum down to a discrete set. That discrete set is what designers tune, test, and exploit.

This page establishes the three fundamental boundary types, derives the mode quantisation condition, applies it to the oblate spheroidal geometry of the [[Psi Stabilizer]], and connects the result to the [[TPMS Lattice Design]] fabrication parameter <math>t</math>.
